                                "markdown": "SQL injection happens when untrusted data is embedded into a SQL string that is executed by a SQL execution API.\nThis rule focuses on the security-sensitive call itself (for example `Statement.executeQuery(...)`, `JdbcTemplate.query(...)`,\nor `EntityManager.createNativeQuery(...)`).\n\nVulnerable example:\n\n```java\nimport java.sql.Connection;\nimport java.sql.ResultSet;\nimport java.sql.Statement;\n\npublic class UserRepository {\n    public ResultSet findById(Connection conn, String userIdFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        // userIdFromRequest is untrusted (source can be Servlet, Spring, etc.)\n        String sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = '\" + userIdFromRequest + \"'\";\n\n        // VULNERABLE: tainted data reaches SQL execution API\n        Statement st = conn.createStatement();\n        return st.executeQuery(sql);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSafe example:\n\n```java\nimport java.sql.Connection;\nimport java.sql.PreparedStatement;\nimport java.sql.ResultSet;\n\npublic class UserRepository {\n    public ResultSet findById(Connection conn, String userIdFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        String sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?\";\n\n        PreparedStatement ps = conn.prepareStatement(sql);\n        ps.setString(1, userIdFromRequest); // bound as data, not SQL syntax\n        return ps.executeQuery();\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey vulnerable patterns covered by this rule include JDBC statement execution, Spring JDBC operations,\nand dynamic JPA/Hibernate query creation when untrusted input controls query text.",
                                "text": "SQL injection happens when untrusted data is embedded into a SQL string that is executed by a SQL execution API.\nThis rule focuses on the security-sensitive call itself (for example `Statement.executeQuery(...)`, `JdbcTemplate.query(...)`,\nor `EntityManager.createNativeQuery(...)`).\n\nVulnerable example:\n\n```java\nimport java.sql.Connection;\nimport java.sql.ResultSet;\nimport java.sql.Statement;\n\npublic class UserRepository {\n    public ResultSet findById(Connection conn, String userIdFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        // userIdFromRequest is untrusted (source can be Servlet, Spring, etc.)\n        String sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = '\" + userIdFromRequest + \"'\";\n\n        // VULNERABLE: tainted data reaches SQL execution API\n        Statement st = conn.createStatement();\n        return st.executeQuery(sql);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSafe example:\n\n```java\nimport java.sql.Connection;\nimport java.sql.PreparedStatement;\nimport java.sql.ResultSet;\n\npublic class UserRepository {\n    public ResultSet findById(Connection conn, String userIdFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        String sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?\";\n\n        PreparedStatement ps = conn.prepareStatement(sql);\n        ps.setString(1, userIdFromRequest); // bound as data, not SQL syntax\n        return ps.executeQuery();\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey vulnerable patterns covered by this rule include JDBC statement execution, Spring JDBC operations,\nand dynamic JPA/Hibernate query creation when untrusted input controls query text."
