                                "markdown": "LDAP injection occurs when untrusted input reaches LDAP query APIs as filter/query text.\nThis rule focuses on LDAP lookup/search calls in JNDI, UnboundID, and Spring LDAP operations.\n\nVulnerable example:\n\n```java\nimport javax.naming.directory.DirContext;\nimport javax.naming.directory.SearchControls;\n\npublic class LdapService {\n    public void find(DirContext ctx, String filterFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        // filterFromRequest is untrusted\n        ctx.search(\"ou=users,dc=example,dc=com\", filterFromRequest, new SearchControls()); // VULNERABLE\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSafe example:\n\n```java\nimport javax.naming.directory.DirContext;\nimport javax.naming.directory.SearchControls;\n\npublic class LdapService {\n    public void findByUid(DirContext ctx, String uidFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        if (uidFromRequest == null || !uidFromRequest.matches(\"[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}\")) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Invalid uid\");\n        }\n\n        String filter = \"(uid={0})\";\n        Object[] args = new Object[]{uidFromRequest};\n        ctx.search(\"ou=users,dc=example,dc=com\", filter, args, new SearchControls());\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey vulnerable patterns covered by this rule include `DirContext/LdapContext.search`, `lookup`,\nUnboundID `LDAPConnection.search`, and Spring LDAP search/lookup APIs with tainted query data.",
                                "text": "LDAP injection occurs when untrusted input reaches LDAP query APIs as filter/query text.\nThis rule focuses on LDAP lookup/search calls in JNDI, UnboundID, and Spring LDAP operations.\n\nVulnerable example:\n\n```java\nimport javax.naming.directory.DirContext;\nimport javax.naming.directory.SearchControls;\n\npublic class LdapService {\n    public void find(DirContext ctx, String filterFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        // filterFromRequest is untrusted\n        ctx.search(\"ou=users,dc=example,dc=com\", filterFromRequest, new SearchControls()); // VULNERABLE\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSafe example:\n\n```java\nimport javax.naming.directory.DirContext;\nimport javax.naming.directory.SearchControls;\n\npublic class LdapService {\n    public void findByUid(DirContext ctx, String uidFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        if (uidFromRequest == null || !uidFromRequest.matches(\"[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}\")) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Invalid uid\");\n        }\n\n        String filter = \"(uid={0})\";\n        Object[] args = new Object[]{uidFromRequest};\n        ctx.search(\"ou=users,dc=example,dc=com\", filter, args, new SearchControls());\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey vulnerable patterns covered by this rule include `DirContext/LdapContext.search`, `lookup`,\nUnboundID `LDAPConnection.search`, and Spring LDAP search/lookup APIs with tainted query data."
