                                "markdown": "External configuration control exists when untrusted input reaches configuration APIs such as\n`Connection.setCatalog(...)`, allowing runtime database-context switching.\n\nVulnerable example:\n\n```java\nimport java.sql.Connection;\n\npublic class TenantDbService {\n    public void selectCatalog(Connection conn, String catalogFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        // catalogFromRequest is untrusted\n        conn.setCatalog(catalogFromRequest); // VULNERABLE\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSafe example:\n\n```java\nimport java.sql.Connection;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\npublic class TenantDbService {\n    private static final Map<String, String> ALLOWED = Map.of(\"tenant-a\", \"tenant_a_db\", \"tenant-b\", \"tenant_b_db\");\n\n    public void selectCatalog(Connection conn, String tenantIdFromAuth) throws Exception {\n        String catalog = ALLOWED.get(tenantIdFromAuth);\n        if (catalog == null) {\n            throw new SecurityException(\"Unknown tenant\");\n        }\n        conn.setCatalog(catalog);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey operation family covered by this rule is catalog switching via JDBC `Connection.setCatalog(...)`.",
                                "text": "External configuration control exists when untrusted input reaches configuration APIs such as\n`Connection.setCatalog(...)`, allowing runtime database-context switching.\n\nVulnerable example:\n\n```java\nimport java.sql.Connection;\n\npublic class TenantDbService {\n    public void selectCatalog(Connection conn, String catalogFromRequest) throws Exception {\n        // catalogFromRequest is untrusted\n        conn.setCatalog(catalogFromRequest); // VULNERABLE\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSafe example:\n\n```java\nimport java.sql.Connection;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\npublic class TenantDbService {\n    private static final Map<String, String> ALLOWED = Map.of(\"tenant-a\", \"tenant_a_db\", \"tenant-b\", \"tenant_b_db\");\n\n    public void selectCatalog(Connection conn, String tenantIdFromAuth) throws Exception {\n        String catalog = ALLOWED.get(tenantIdFromAuth);\n        if (catalog == null) {\n            throw new SecurityException(\"Unknown tenant\");\n        }\n        conn.setCatalog(catalog);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey operation family covered by this rule is catalog switching via JDBC `Connection.setCatalog(...)`."
